      "refersTo": "release-chain",
      "description": "ReleaseChain in src/components/workspace/DeliveryOverview.tsx, styled in src/index.css. Illustrative states demonstrate independent conditions, not current milestone data.",
      "html": "<ol class=\"ds-release-chain\" aria-label=\"Example release conditions\"><li class=\"ds-chain-item ds-is-ready\"><span class=\"ds-chain-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><svg width=\"12\" height=\"12\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M20 6 9 17l-5-5\"/></svg></span><span>Invoice</span><strong>Paid</strong></li><li class=\"ds-chain-item\"><span class=\"ds-chain-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-chain-dot\"></span></span><span>Materials</span><strong>Not staged</strong></li><li class=\"ds-chain-item\"><span class=\"ds-chain-node\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"ds-chain-dot\"></span></span><span>Predecessors</span><strong>Unfinished</strong></li></ol>",
      "css": ".ds-release-chain{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);list-style:none;padding:0;margin:24px 0;color:var(--text,#202326);font:400 12px/1.5 var(--font,Geist,system-ui,sans-serif)}.ds-chain-item{position:relative;padding-top:28px;font-size:12px}.ds-chain-item:before{content:'';position:absolute;top:8px;left:0;right:0;height:1px;background:var(--line-strong,#b9c0c6)}.ds-chain-item:last-child:before{display:none}.ds-chain-node{position:absolute;top:0;left:0;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;height:17px;width:17px;border:1px solid var(--line-strong,#b9c0c6);border-radius:50%;background:var(--surface,#ffffff)}.ds-chain-dot{width:4px;height:4px;background:var(--text-muted,#626a72);border-radius:50%}.ds-is-ready .ds-chain-node{background:var(--primary,#24282c);color:var(--on-primary,#ffffff);border-color:var(--primary,#24282c)}.ds-chain-item strong{display:block;font-weight:400;color:var(--text-muted,#626a72);margin-top:3px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Delivery ledger",
    "overview": "Drawing-register clarity defines the chosen world: cool paper, graphite text, ink controls, blue schedule marks, and restrained state signals. Compact Geist typography, aligned figures, and flat sheets keep milestone readiness and financial evidence readable together.\n\nThe primary workspaces use an open-plane shell and purposeful registers rather than nested decorative cards. Existing dialogs and embedded tools are brought into this world through compatibility styles and theme bridges; their retained utility markup is not the template for new workspace components.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light-first surfaces with a persistent dark appearance.",
      "Labelled navigation, compact controls, and fluid workspace gutters.",
      "Tabular financial evidence and explicit status wording.",
      "Flat panels with restrained borders; elevation reserved for overlays.",
      "A three-part release chain for invoice, materials, and predecessors."
    ],
    "rules": [
      { "name": "The State Has Words Rule", "body": "Pair semantic color with a visible state label; a colored dot or track is not the only explanation.", "section": "colors" },
      { "name": "The Tabular Evidence Rule", "body": "Use Geist tabular numerals for money and align numeric table columns to the right; do not substitute a decorative mono face.", "section": "typography" },
      { "name": "The Flat Sheet Rule", "body": "Use surface tone and borders for workspace hierarchy; reserve elevation for overlays.", "section": "elevation" }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the light/dark CSS-variable pairs from `src/index.css` for new workspace surfaces.",
      "**Do** keep financial columns right-aligned with Geist tabular numerals.",
      "**Do** pair state color with readable labels and keep invoice, materials, and predecessors distinct.",
      "**Do** preserve the navigation fold, mobile register layout, visible focus, and reduced-motion behavior.",
      "**Do** keep selected-milestone evidence visibly separate from the named recovery proposal."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** add gradients or decorative workspace shadows; reserve depth for overlays.",
      "**Don't** promote legacy dialog utilities, FinOps palette entries, or third-party defaults into primary workspace tokens.",
      "**Don't** make pending approval look like completed payment or release readiness.",
      "**Don't** invent financial values, progress percentages, savings totals, or verification claims to fill the interface.",
      "**Don't** show chart-only controls when the mobile schedule chart is hidden."
    ]
  }
}
